From 99248a65198e9b4778b7ce0b8388a6fd35f26640 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:56:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] stage 280: identity and situation are two channels, not
 one sum

283 answered the question the other way round from my prediction. Bare
anchors barely crowd - nearest-other cosine p50 0.793, only 0.018 of them
at tau - while the summed address key crowds at 0.345. The context is not
what saves the address, it is what fills the space: every English
sentence has much the same character statistics, so adding a context
fingerprint pulls every key toward one mean.

So the two stay apart. --addr-key two scores a mention by the MINIMUM of
its anchor cosine and its context cosine, where neither channel can drag
the other and both have to agree, and it is the default now. set (members
kept, channels summed) and mean (the original) remain as arms.

Also settles the coverage question: --k-gap 0.35 against 0.0 at the same
rung changes precision 0.6638 -> 0.6625, recall 0.7714 -> 0.7717 and mean
candidates 3.996 -> 4.005. The cut was doing nothing; the missing witnesses
are vote recall, which is the same failure the return path had before it
stopped ranking.

The write side still merges on the summed key - fp_addresses in 279 is
where foreign_member_rate 0.052 comes from - and is not touched here.

